      "findings": "As of 2024, the population of London reached a new high of approximately 9.1 million people. This follows a period of steady growth since the early 1990s, when the population had declined to a low of 6.8 million in 1991.\n\nDemographic analysis indicates that London's population is generally younger than the rest of England. Specifically, Inner London has a notably high proportion of residents aged between 25 and 34, with over half of its population falling within the age range of early twenties to early forties."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:3",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the current population of Paris?",
      "sources": [
